        </div>
        <div id="weatherResult" style="margin-top:16px"></div>
        <p id="weatherNote" style="font-size:12px;opacity:.85;margin-top:10px">Demo data for learning. In Lesson 39 below, learn how to connect real OpenWeatherMap API.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>3. What is fetch()?</h2>
    <p><b>fetch(url) = Go and get data from that URL.</b> It returns a Promise - It takes some time, because data comes from internet. So we must wait for it.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Way 1 - .then() - Old way, still used</span><br>
<span class="text">fetch("https://api.example.com/weather?city=Lahore")</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">.then(response => response.json()) // Convert to JSON</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">.then(data => {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log(data); // Full weather data</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log(data.main.temp); // Temperature</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">})</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">.catch(error => { console.log("Error: " + error); });</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Way 2 - async / await - New way, easier to read</span><br>
<span class="text">async function getWeather() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let response = await fetch("https://api.example.com/weather?city=Lahore");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let data = await response.json(); // Wait, then convert to JSON</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log(data.main.temp);</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">getWeather();</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Memory Trick:</b> <code>await</code> = Wait here until data comes. You can only use <code>await</code> inside an <code>async</code> function. <code>fetch()</code> gives Response, <code>.json()</code> gives real Data.</div>
    <h2>4. What Does Weather API Return? - JSON</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Real OpenWeatherMap response - It is one big object</span><br>
<span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">"name": "Lahore",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">"main": { "temp": 32, "humidity": 45, "feels_like": 34 },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">"weather": [ { "main": "Clear", "description": "clear sky", "icon": "01d" } ],</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">"wind": { "speed": 5.2 }</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// How to read it:</span><br>
<span class="text">data.name // "Lahore"</span><br>
<span class="text">data.main.temp // 32</span><br>
<span class="text">data.main.humidity // 45</span><br>
<span class="text">data.weather[0].main // "Clear"</span><br>
<span class="text">data.weather[0].description // "clear sky"</span><br>
<span class="text">data.wind.speed // 5.2</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. Complete Example - Real Weather App With API</h2>
    <p>Steps to get real data: 1. Go to openweathermap.org - Sign up free. 2. Copy your API Key. 3. Paste key in code below where it says YOUR_API_KEY.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">Weather App</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"city"</span> <span class="attr">placeholder</span>=<span class="val">"Type city"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"getWeather()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Search</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"result"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let API_KEY = "YOUR_API_KEY"; // Paste your key here</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">async function getWeather() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let city = document.getElementById("city").value.trim();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (city === "") { alert("Please type a city!"); return; }</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("result").innerText = "Loading... ⏳";</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">try {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let url = `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?q=${city}&appid=${API_KEY}&units=metric`;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let response = await fetch(url);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (!response.ok) { throw new Error("City not found!"); }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let data = await response.json();</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = `</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;h2&gt;${data.name} - ${data.main.temp}°C&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;p&gt;${data.weather[0].description}&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">&lt;p&gt;Humidity: ${data.main.humidity}% | Wind: ${data.wind.speed} km/h&lt;/p&gt;`;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">} catch (error) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("result").innerText = "❌ " + error.message;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span> <span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. API vs LocalStorage - Difference</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Feature</th><th>API (fetch)</th><th>LocalStorage</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Where is data?</td><td>On server / Internet</td><td>In your browser</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Needs internet?</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Data changes?</td><td>Yes - Live data, updates every time</td><td>No - Only what you saved</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Example</td><td>Weather, News, Maps, YouTube videos</td><td>Theme, Notes, Cart, Name</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>7. Common Errors</h2>
    <p>1. <b>City not found:</b> Check spelling. API returns 404. Always use try/catch and check <code>response.ok</code>.<br>2. <b>Forgot await:</b> Without await, you get a Promise, not data. <code>await fetch()</code> and <code>await response.json()</code> - Both need await.<br>3. <b>Forgot async:</b> You cannot use await in a normal function. Function must start with <code>async function</code>.</p>
    <h2>8. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. Quote App - Use fetch to https://api.quotable.io/random - Show random quote + author on button click<br>2. Real Weather - Sign up on openweathermap.org, get free API key, connect real API like example above<br>3. Joke App - Use fetch to https://official-joke-api.appspot.com/random_joke - Show setup + punchline</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> API = Waiter - Ask server, get data | fetch(url) = Get data from URL | await = Wait until data comes, only inside async function | response.json() = Convert response to JSON object | data.main.temp = Temperature in API data | try/catch = If city wrong or net off, show error not crash | units=metric = Temperature in °C, not Fahrenheit</div>
