          <div class="question"><b>Q1. What is an API?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> A waiter - Ask server, get data back</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> A color</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> A loop</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> A database in browser</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. What does fetch(url) do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> Gets data from that URL</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> Saves data</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> Deletes data</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> Changes color</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. What does await do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> Waits until data comes, then continues</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> Deletes data</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> Stops page</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. Where can you use await?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> Only inside async function</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> Anywhere</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> Only in HTML</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> Only in CSS</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. How to convert fetch response to data?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> await response.json()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> response.text()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> response.data()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> response.get()</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. In weather data, how to get temperature?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> data.main.temp</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> data.temp</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> data.temperature</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> data.weather.temp</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. How to get weather description?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> data.weather[0].description</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> data.description</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> data.main.description</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> data.weather.description</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. What does units=metric do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> Temperature in °C (Celsius)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> Temperature in °F</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> Temperature in Kelvin</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> No temperature</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. Why use try/catch with fetch?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> If city wrong or net off, show error not crash</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> To make faster</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> To add color</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> No reason</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q10. API vs LocalStorage - Which needs internet?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="a"> API needs internet, LocalStorage does not</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="b"> Both need internet</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="c"> LocalStorage needs internet</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="d"> Neither needs internet</label></div>
          <button type="button" class="btn" onclick="checkTest(false)">Submit Test - Check Result</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-next" onclick="resetTest()">Try Again</button>
        </form>
